<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  GamorreanXenotype.xml                      Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  ===============
  cherry_picker_killlist.md §2 records the standing decision: "author a CUSTOM
  Gamorrean race... not just a label swap; we build our own xenotype... as the
  Hutts' pig-soldier stock." This is that xenotype.

  It supersedes the earlier "derived from Pigskin" framing. Pigskin is a vanilla
  Biotech xenotype with no Star Wars content; the two Gamorreans already in the
  load set (guy762_xenotype_gamorrean and BTD_Gamorrean) are strictly better
  starting points, being purpose-built for the setting. This def is forked from
  guy762_xenotype_gamorrean, which is the more coherent of the two.

  WHAT WAS INHERITED UNCHANGED
  ============================
  23 of guy762's 24 genes, verbatim. Every one was confirmed present in the live
  DefDump before this file was written; none is guessed. That deliberately keeps
  the upstream authors' balance intact rather than silently rebalancing a
  species someone else tuned.

  THE TWO DELIBERATE CHANGES
  ==========================
  1. ADDED Ears_Pig. This is the single biggest appearance win available with
     zero new art. Vanilla Biotech ships drooping pig ears as an overlay gene,
     with art already packed in the base game, and neither existing Gamorrean
     uses it. Drooping ears widen the silhouette in the south AND north views,
     which is exactly where the current version reads as a bald human.

  2. REMOVED Headbone_MiniHorns. Gamorreans have tusks, not horns. Composited
     against the real head art, the mini-horns read as outward-pointing devil
     horns and fight the porcine silhouette rather than supporting it. This is a
     taste call, clearly flagged: re-add the single <li>Headbone_MiniHorns</li>
     line below to restore upstream behaviour exactly.

  ⚠️ OPEN QUESTION — BODY SIZE CONTRADICTS THE SCALE ATLAS (raised 2026-08-11)
  ============================================================================
  `worldbuilding/star_wars_species_scale_reference_atlas.pdf` puts the Gamorrean
  at **1.3–1.6 m — SHORTER than the 1.80 m human standard**, sourced from
  swrpggm.com. This def inherits `guy762_BodySizeGene_big` from upstream, which
  says the opposite.

  Both readings have support: Wookieepedia opens with "a species of tall, strong
  bipeds", while the RPG stat lines the atlas cites are consistently sub-human.
  Screen Gamorreans read as broad and heavy rather than tall.

  Deliberately NOT changed here — body size is a balance lever (it feeds
  combatPower, melee reach and carrying capacity), and silently shrinking the
  Hutts' door-muscle is a campaign decision, not a cleanup. If we want the atlas
  reading, swap `guy762_BodySizeGene_big` for a small/medium body-size gene and
  keep `Body_Fat`: short, wide and thick is closer to the films than tall.

  WHAT THIS DOES NOT YET FIX
  ==========================
  The head itself. Jaw_Heavy carries forcedHeadTypes = Male_HeavyJawNormal /
  Female_HeavyJawNormal, so a Gamorrean wears a VANILLA heavy-jaw human skull
  with a flat pig-nose decal on it. There is no species head gene, for either
  Gamorrean, in any of the three xenotype mods; verified against the live
  GeneDef dump, not inferred.

  That is the gap the commissioned art fills (see image_request/graphic.md).
  When the six head PNGs land, add a Jawa_Head_Gamorrean gene with
  forcedHeadTypes pointing at new HeadTypeDefs, and drop Jaw_Heavy from the list
  below so the two do not fight over the head slot.

  DUPLICATES
  ==========
  This makes three Gamorrean xenotypes in the picker. Intentional for now: ours
  is the one the pawnkinds use, and deleting the other two is a Cherry Picker
  action taken at campaign setup, not a def change. Tracked in
  cherry_picker_killlist.md §2.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <XenotypeDef>
    <defName>Jawa_Xeno_Gamorrean</defName>
    <label>Gamorrean</label>
    <description>A species of tall, strong bipeds from the Outer Rim world of Gamorr. Gamorreans have porcine traits: an upturned, large-nostriled cartilaginous snout, heavy jowls, drooping ears and upturned tusks. Their hulking bodies are covered in thick, hairless green hide.\n\nSlow of thought and quick to violence, they are prized off-world as muscle. The Hutt kajidics buy them by the crate, arm them with axes their own smiths could not have forged, and post them at every door worth guarding.</description>
    <descriptionShort>Hulking green pig-humanoids from Gamorr. Slow, ugly, hyper-aggressive and enormously strong — the Hutts' preferred door-muscle.</descriptionShort>
    <inheritable>true</inheritable>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/Pigskin</iconPath>
    <combatPowerFactor>1.7</combatPowerFactor>
    <nameMaker>KoTOR_NamerGamorrean</nameMaker>
    <chanceToUseNameMaker>1</chanceToUseNameMaker>
    <genes>
      <!-- appearance -->
      <li>guy762_Face_jowls</li>
      <li>guy762_Face_tusks</li>
      <li>Ears_Pig</li>                          <!-- ADDED: see header -->
      <li>Nose_Pig</li>
      <li>Jaw_Heavy</li>                         <!-- forces the vanilla heavy-jaw head; replace when our head gene exists -->
      <li>Brow_Heavy</li>
      <li>Hair_BaldOnly</li>
      <li>Beard_NoBeardOnly</li>
      <li>Beauty_VeryUgly</li>
      <li>Skin_Green</li>
      <li>guy762_Skin_DarkGreen</li>
      <li>Body_Fat</li>
      <li>guy762_BodySizeGene_big</li>
      <li>VoicePig</li>
      <!-- <li>Headbone_MiniHorns</li> -->       <!-- REMOVED: see header; uncomment to restore upstream -->

      <!-- temperament -->
      <li>Aggression_HyperAggressive</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Turn_Gene_HerdMentality</li>
      <li>Turn_Gene_VerySlowNeuralHeat</li>
      <li>GS_Primitive</li>
      <li>AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual</li>

      <!-- constitution -->
      <li>Robust</li>
      <li>MeleeDamage_Strong</li>
      <li>Unstoppable</li>
      <li>StrongStomach</li>
      <li>RobustDigestion</li>
    </genes>
  </XenotypeDef>

</Defs>
